# Files that run or are read on a Linux server (deploy/relay) keep LF line endings,
# whatever core.autocrlf says: bash fails on CRLF.
deploy/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
# Pictures are never text, inside deploy/ too (the landing page's): converting line endings
# in one corrupts it.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
# Written by tauri-build on every build, always with LF: checked out the same, so a build on
# Windows (core.autocrlf, as on GitHub's runners) leaves them as committed. The release
# workflow's Windows build refuses a tree the build changed (M26c).
apps/desktop/src-tauri/permissions/autogenerated/*.toml text eol=lf
